t or far right  president of France being elected where  does the UK election sit in that list of  concerns  nuki election actually I think fits  quite low down on that list because  markets are there's so much going on in  the political sphere there are so many  curveballs coming out of left field that  markets in a way becoming quite immune  the reaction periods are very very short  no to new events that are coming out so  I think short of a very major surprise  like a major configuration in North  Korea or something particularly  unexpected coming out of the French  particularly the first round of the  French presidential elections this  coming weekend I think actually markets  are tending to shrug off some of these  political factors  and in the grand scheme of things when  you look at where the UK fits and all of  that frankly markets don't think it's  very important it's quite far down the  list
 

